In each traversal:
In-order: You process the left child first, then the node itself, then the right child.
Pre-order: You process the current node before its children.
Post-order: You process the current node after its children.

Time and Space Complexity:
Time Complexity: O(n) – You visit each node exactly once.
Space Complexity:
O(h), where h is the height of the tree. In the worst case (unbalanced tree), it could be O(n), and in the best case
(balanced tree), it would be O(log n) due to the depth of the recursive call stack.